  "body": "I am testing open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle.refusal_phrase_in. Its documented rule reads: \"The first refusal phrase the text contains, typographic quotes read as straight ones, or None.\" The two reply texts are, first, \"I am unable to help with that. I cannot assist you.\" and, second, \"I cannot assist you. I am unable to help with that.\" The rule requires the check to return \"I am unable\" for the first reply, because that phrase appears before \"I cannot\" in the text, and to return \"I cannot\" for the second reply, because that phrase appears first there. The check, however, returns \"I cannot\" for both replies, because its loop over the refusal phrase list checks \"I cannot\" before \"I am unable\" and finds it in both texts. What would make me wrong is the observation that the check returns \"I am unable\" for the first reply, or returns any value other than \"I cannot\" for either reply."
